    {
      "id": "claim_61f4fcb2535d481a921750ddc32833f3",
      "statement": "The data store is an H2 in-memory database (jdbc:h2:mem:tmall_ssh;MODE=MySQL;DB_CLOSE_DELAY=-1) that is re-created and re-seeded from classpath:sql/tmall_ssh_h2.sql by the Spring dbInit bean at every context refresh, so rows written during a session are discarded on restart while the demo data is restored.",
